      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-381",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 5 \\cdot 9^x +3 e^x \\, \\textrm d x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int 5 \\cdot 9^x +3 e^x  \\, \\textrm d x &= \\displaystyle 5\\int 9^x \\, \\textrm{d}x+ 3 \\displaystyle \\int e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n&= 5\\cdot \\dfrac{9^x}{\\ln 9} + 3 e^x +C.\n}\n$$"
    },
