        ":question/id": "bf1d61d4-5576-5207-ad64-f8866ebc8219",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-31261",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int ({e}^{x}+{8}^{x}+\\frac{3}{x})\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({e}^{x}+{8}^{x}+\\frac{3}{x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {8}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}+\\frac{{8}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}8}+3\\operatorname{ln}|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
