        ":question/problem": "$\\int ({5}^{x}-2{e}^{x}+2)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({5}^{x}-2{e}^{x}+2)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{x}}{ln\u20615}-2{e}^{x}+2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
